Verification status:

* [x] MMS verification infrastructure
* [x] Second-order upwind refinement study
* [x] Upwind behavior verified
* [x] Central differencing verified
* [x] Second-order convergence demonstrated with Central reconstruction/convection
* [x] Second-order upwind verified

Important numerical observation:

* Upwind currently exhibits approximately first-order convergence, as expected
* Central/reconstructed formulation demonstrates approximately second-order convergence
* Second-order upwind demonstrates approximately second-order convergence on both Convective2D and AdvectionDiffusion2D
* Higher-order convection work should preserve this verification framework
* Boundary-adjacent upwind cells use first-order upwind fallback when a second-order upstream stencil cannot be constructed

### Second-Order Upwind Verification

Representative refinement results:

Convective2D
    Observed L2 order   ≈ 2.00071
    Observed Linf order ≈ 1.99881
    Status                PASS

AdvectionDiffusion2D
    Observed L2 order   ≈ 1.9582
    Observed Linf order ≈ 1.94134
    Status                PASS

The second-order-upwind reconstruction therefore satisfies the expected second-order asymptotic behavior for the current verification cases.

The reconstruction also has an explicit boundary fallback:

Second-order upstream stencil available

                ↓
    φ_f = 1.5 φ_U - 0.5 φ_UU

No upstream cell available
    
                ↓
            φ_f = φ_U


The fallback is verified independently at the stencil level.

